       function  falls back to the use of ssyymmlliinnkk().  When _l_i_n_k_p_a_t_h is a rela‐
       tive pathname, glibc constructs a pathname based on the  symbolic  link
       in _/_p_r_o_c_/_s_e_l_f_/_f_d that corresponds to the _n_e_w_d_i_r_f_d argument.

